{{/*
  ~/.tmux/plugins is tpm's install directory, not ours. bootstrap.sh clones tpm
  itself, dot_tmux.conf names the plugins and the version to pin them at, and
  tpm fetches the rest — so the tree is fully reproducible from two files.

  It used to be checked in: 246 of the repo's 330 tracked files and 4.2MB were
  three vendored clones, .git directories and packfiles included. Beyond the
  bulk, chezmoi managing them means it fights tpm: after a `prefix + U` the
  plugin is newer than the source, and `chezmoi apply` reverts it.

  Ignored rather than merely deleted, so `chezmoi add` cannot pull them back.
*/ -}}
.tmux/plugins/**

{{/*
  Machine-specific inclusion. This file is always evaluated as a template — no
  .tmpl suffix — so a path can be skipped per machine. Paths here are *target*
  names (.config/i3), not source names (dot_config/i3).

  i3 and i3status are the window manager and its status bar: Linux only. Only
  fontconfig looked like a candidate to join them, and it turns out to be
  present on macOS too.
*/ -}}
